{
  "slug": "truinorva-triz",
  "name": "Truinorva Triz",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A comprehensive TRIZ toolkit that turns Claude into a structured innovation partner. 26 model-invoked skills covering system framing (ISQ, MPV, 9 Boxes), function analysis, root-cause and root-conflict analysis, contradiction resolution (40 Inventive Principles, separation, 76 Standard Solutions), resources, ideality, trimming, and patent analysis. Built for R&D engineers, product managers, and innovation consultants who want methodology, not random brainstorming.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **26 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (26): `76-standard-solutions` (TRIZ 76 Standard Solutions — guides users through solving technical and organizational problems using Substance-Field Analysis (Su-Field) and…), `business-function-analysis` (Non-Engineer Function Analysis using simplified TRIZ — helps users from non-engineering backgrounds apply Function Analysis to improve systems…), `business-msd` (TRIZ Multi-Screen Diagram (MSD / 9 Boxes / 9 Windows) for business and technical systems), `cause-effect-chain-analysis` (TRIZ Cause and Effect Chain Analysis (CECA) and Root Cause Analysis (RCA) — guides users through structured root…), `contradiction-solver` (TRIZ Contradiction Solver and 40 Inventive Principles — resolves engineering and physical contradictions using the Altshuller Matrix, Matrix…), `derivative-resources` (TRIZ Derivative Resources Analysis — identifies not only existing resources but also potential derivative resources that arise through…), `feature-transfer` (TRIZ Feature Transfer — helps enhance systems by adopting beneficial features from alternative systems), `function-analysis` (TRIZ Function Analysis for technical systems — identifies tools, actions, objects, and functions, clarifies component relationships, and reveals…), and 18 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install truinorva-triz@claude-community` from `jenson500/truinorva-triz`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
